# Polythene Pam, outro (figure 187.3)
# Twenty-two bars: eight times the two-bar double plagal phrase (D and A, two beats each, then a
# bar of E), then six bars of E, then the A that begins the next track. The numbers over the typed
# chart count the iterations and the six E bars; they are kept as bar marks.
# The "Bassline:" in the typed chart is a label, not notes: the bassline is the downward scale
# E D C# B in bars 3-6 of the E section, one note to a bar, leading to the A. Pollack's "I" under
# the A marks it as the new tonic (E heard as V of A).
# Added: the bass E in E-bars 1-2 and the A at the end are not typed; they are the chord roots
# (Pollack says the outro's phrase has "the root note of each chord in the bassline").
# Bass for the double plagal iterations is left to the chords.
#? Bass octave of the scale (E3 down to A2) is chosen for range; check against the record.
key E

